{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick","id":1447854,"title":"Save a Sleeper with Vulgar Magick","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-07T15:35:05-07:00","id":1447854,"title":"Save a Sleeper with Vulgar Magick","content":"What happens when you use Vulgar Magick in front of witnesses to save a Sleeper from death?<br /> <br /> 1. Death by a mundane cause.<br /> 2. Death by Magick.<br /> 3. Death at the hands of a Spirit who has breached the Gauntlet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":".  grammar 05-10-2021, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T15:40:11-07:00","id":1447855,"title":"","content":"I feel like I'm missing something here. Why wouldn't the result just be, &quot;take Paradox per your roll?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T16:20:30-07:00","id":1447859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1447855#post1447855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like I'm missing something here. Why wouldn't the result just be, &quot;take Paradox per your roll?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Does the paradox kill the Sleeper?<br /> What does the person who was saved remember?<br /> What do people remember happening?<br /> Is there any circumstance under which Paradox &quot;forgives&quot; the use of Vulgar Magick to save a Sleeper? What if were a thousand Sleepers who were saved?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T16:46:28-07:00","id":1447863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1447859#post1447859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the paradox kill the Sleeper?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Paradox generally only impacts the mage casting the effect.<br /> <br /> You can kill a Sleeper (or anyone really) with Paradox by modifying their Pattern in a fashion that causes Pattern Bleed with a long enough duration, but that doesn't apply to the situation you've posted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What does the person who was saved remember?<br /> What do people remember happening? </div> </div> </div>Whatever they saw, but they'll tend to try to rationalize it as best they can. And there's strong odds someone will alter their memories since both the Technocracy and Traditions don't want Sleepers running around with memories of vulgar magic if the memories would cause larger problems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there any circumstance under which Paradox &quot;forgives&quot; the use of Vulgar Magick to save a Sleeper? What if were a thousand Sleepers who were saved? </div> </div> </div>Paradox isn't a thinking entity, it's a function of reality. While Paradox might result in a Paradox spirit, which might have thoughts about what to do with a mage, Paradox itself doesn't care why you do what you do. If you use vulgar magic to save one life, or 1,000 lives, you take whatever Paradox you take, and then deal with the consequences. Paradox is not a moral force that makes moral judgements.<br /> <br /> I am still very confused, because you seem to have a number of assumptions and I have no idea where they're coming from.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T16:49:24-07:00","id":1447864,"title":"","content":"I think Horizon thinks that if you use vulgar magic in front of many witnesses the magic fails automatically.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T17:16:03-07:00","id":1447870,"title":"","content":"What would be the point of vulgar with witnesses having a roll with a difficulty established by the books if it automatically failed? Like I said, I feel like there's assumptions being made, and I'm not sure where they're coming from. There are rules for casting vulgar magic with witnesses... some assumption would have to be getting in the way to assume that automatically fails despite having rules for how not to fail at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T17:33:14-07:00","id":1447872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1447859#post1447859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Does the paradox kill the Sleeper?<br /> What does the person who was saved remember?<br /> What do people remember happening?<br /> Is there any circumstance under which Paradox &quot;forgives&quot; the use of Vulgar Magick to save a Sleeper? What if were a thousand Sleepers who were saved?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, unless the Storyteller decides to force a Paradox roll at that moment and have the Paradox take a form that distorts the spell and kills the Sleeper (or lets them die from whatever was going to kill them previously) - but I\u2019d only do that with player consent for drama for their character, it\u2019s certainly not the default for Paradox.<br /> <br /> they remember what happened. Sleepers not remembering Awakened Magic is a Mage the Awakening thing, not Mage the Ascenson<br /> <br /> see above<br /> <br /> no, the Consensus has no moral parameters. Vulgar with witnesses is Vulgar with witnesses.<br /> <br /> Number of witnesses has no effect above one RAW. This is a slight problem of mechanics matching lore and some people tweak it, but RAW, other than the difference between \u201c0\u201d and \u201cany\u201d, number of witnesses is mechanically irrelevant","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-07-2021, 08:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T17:51:15-07:00","id":1447874,"title":"","content":"Well... one caveat. Reality Zones. If the the local Consensus specifically allows for life saving miracles, performing a life saving miracle might be coincidental. Choristers praying in a manner consistent with the local dominant faith to call down a miracle, are the most likely to benefit from this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-09T15:24:51-07:00","id":1448076,"title":"","content":"If you think rolling the dice and having reality snap you with a newspaper is worth saving a life","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T10:53:25-07:00","id":1448145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1447863#post1447863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am still very confused, because you seem to have a number of assumptions and I have no idea where they're coming from.</div> </div> </div> </div>I formulated the post in the form of a question. The idea is to clarify some things I am having trouble with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1447863#post1447863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whatever they saw, but they'll tend to try to rationalize it as best they can. And there's strong odds someone will alter their memories since both the Technocracy and Traditions don't want Sleepers running around with memories of vulgar magic if the memories would cause larger problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that when Paradox comes to repair reality, it blurs Sleepers' memories. If it is mainly NWO Operatives having to run around editing the memory of every Sleeper who witnessed something, the Traditions *would* want to leave lasting memories of Vulgar Magick. As long as the Operatives are occupied with a constant massive cover up, they have way less time to spy on and assassinate Tradition Mages. It is worth the cost in terms of a few points of Paradox to produce an event that forces Blacksuits to show up at a specific location and repeatedly Mindwipe people. I do not see how the Technocracy could function without Paradox acting on the memories of witnesses. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T11:01:32-07:00","id":1448146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1447864#post1447864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Horizon thinks that if you use vulgar magic in front of many witnesses the magic fails automatically.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not the effect, but any memory of it that would change the Consensus. It seems any Player willing to pay the mechanical cost in Paradox can start destroying the Consensus. You can build your character to avoid the consequences with Arcane, Familiar and Prime to cloak your Resonance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T11:04:24-07:00","id":1448147,"title":"","content":"Paradox does not blur sleepers memories. That's something in mage the awakening, not Mage the ascension. It's also a thing in changeling the dreaming, and in Werewolf the apocalypse. But no, Paradox does not cloud sleepers minds in mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T11:12:03-07:00","id":1448148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1447872#post1447872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Number of witnesses has no effect above one RAW. This is a slight problem of mechanics matching lore and some people tweak it, but RAW, other than the difference between \u201c0\u201d and \u201cany\u201d, number of witnesses is mechanically irrelevant</div> </div> </div> </div>What I get from this is that the game I love is totally absurd, rules wise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T11:33:20-07:00","id":1448150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448147#post1448147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paradox does not blur sleepers memories. That's something in mage the awakening, not Mage the ascension. It's also a thing in changeling the dreaming, and in Werewolf the apocalypse. But no, Paradox does not cloud sleepers minds in mage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> About the only thing from Awakening that appeals to me. Where, in Ascension, is the incentive to slowly use coincidental effects to change the Consensus?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T11:40:04-07:00","id":1448152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448148#post1448148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">What I get from this is that the game I love is totally absurd, rules wise. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Here's how I tweak the rules to make it fit the setting more.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Coincidental and Vulgar-without-Witnesses work as in M20 rules.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Successful Vulgar-With-Witnesses gives you the rating of the highest Sphere used in the effect in Paradox MULTIPLIED BY THE NUMBER OF DIGITS in the Sleeper count. So if your effect has hundreds of sleeper witnesses, you triple the Paradox. A thousand you multiply by 4, etc.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448148#post1448148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I get from this is that the game I love is totally absurd, rules wise.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You can try, but that would be hard with coincidental effects. If the rules reflected the setting, the problem with using Vulgar effects to alter the consensus is that doing it on a big enough scale is suicidal (see my above suggested hack). But RAW the single point of paradox you'd take for a feat of vulgar magic witnessed by millions would be worth the effort (hence my hack).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T11:50:15-07:00","id":1448154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448150#post1448150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> About the only thing from Awakening that appeals to me. Where, in Ascension, is the incentive to slowly use coincidental effects to change the Consensus?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's plenty of incentive to slowly use coincidental effects, from the lower difficulty to the complete absence of paradox buildup when you go coincidental. And there's plenty of incentive to change the consensus. Because if a reality Zone says something is coincidental, you get to do it without having to worry about paradox.<br /> <br /> The only thing lacking is a specific and explicit combination of the two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T12:03:29-07:00","id":1448155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448152#post1448152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Here's how I tweak the rules to make it fit the setting more.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Coincidental and Vulgar-without-Witnesses work as in M20 rules.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Successful Vulgar-With-Witnesses gives you the rating of the highest Sphere used in the effect in Paradox MULTIPLIED BY THE NUMBER OF DIGITS in the Sleeper count. So if your effect has hundreds of sleeper witnesses, you triple the Paradox. A thousand you multiply by 4, etc.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You can try, but that would be hard with coincidental effects. If the rules reflected the setting, the problem with using Vulgar effects to alter the consensus is that doing it on a big enough scale is suicidal (see my above suggested hack). But RAW the single point of paradox you'd take for a feat of vulgar magic witnessed by millions would be worth the effort (hence my hack).</div> </div> </div> </div>That is sensible homebrew. Some kind of hack is required to make Ascension playable. I would be curious to know what percentage storytellers use RAW and if homebrew adaptations all attempt to address a common set of inconsistencies between the rules and the setting.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T12:03:37-07:00","id":1448156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448148#post1448148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I get from this is that the game I love is totally absurd, rules wise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess this really depends on your intuition about what is going on when a sleeper sees Vulgar magic. If the sleeper is adding to the conflict between the magic and reality then, yes, VWW should get fiercer the more actual witnesses there are. That's perfectly workable.<br /> <br /> The way I view it, though, is that if the magic is Vulgar reality is already broadly set against it. The witness isn't adding to the weight of reality he is focusing it. Reality was already pushing in the opposite direction to the Mage, now it is pushing directly against the Mage. Adding yet more witnesses doesn't really change anything beyond that.<br /> <br /> It's up to you if you want to use the former reasoning and house rule it.<br /> <br /> As far as people forgetting Magic, I think it is mentioned in the books here and there that people often rationalize away the impossible. They don't forget the event, per se, they just latch onto an explanation they can understand. It is certainly in keeping with the setting, but there is no mechanic to make it happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T12:12:41-07:00","id":1448158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448156#post1448156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess this really depends on your intuition about what is going on when a sleeper sees Vulgar magic. If the sleeper is adding to the conflict between the magic and reality then, yes, VWW should get fiercer the more actual witnesses there are. That's perfectly workable.<br /> <br /> The way I view it, though, is that if the magic is Vulgar reality is already broadly set against it. The witness isn't adding to the weight of reality he is focusing it. Reality was already pushing in the opposite direction to the Mage, now it is pushing directly against the Mage. Adding yet more witnesses doesn't really change anything beyond that.<br /> <br /> It's up to you if you want to use the former reasoning and house rule it.<br /> <br /> As far as people forgetting Magic, I think it is mentioned in the books here and there that people often rationalize away the impossible. They don't forget the event, per se, they just latch onto an explanation they can understand. It is certainly in keeping with the setting, but there is no mechanic to make it happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would add that between Victorian mage and Mage made easy, there's a push to remove witnesses as a factor, with vulgar and vulgar with witnesses being replaced by uncanny and extreme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T12:21:21-07:00","id":1448160,"title":"","content":"Also, Awakening has a lot to recommend it, even if you prefer ascensions metaphysics. Specifically, a lot of the changes to the mechanics of how magic works in practice were motivated by a desire to fix deficiency that the developers had with ascension. I would recommend that you could get a fair amount of mileage out of taking Awakening and the mage translation guide and using the latter to incorporate elements from the former into ascension.<br /> <br /> Note that I'm thinking specifically of the first edition of awakened. The second edition took steps to make itself different from Ascension, whereas the first edition was written as a replacement for ascension. This leads to some differences between the two editions, with the first edition having more in common with Ascension then the second edition has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T12:24:04-07:00","id":1448162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448155#post1448155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is sensible homebrew. Some kind of hack is required to make Ascension playable. I would be curious to know what percentage storytellers use RAW and if homebrew adaptations all attempt to address a common set of inconsistencies between the rules and the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, I would take some issue with the idea that some sort of hack is needed in order to make Ascension playable. I will agree, though, that it relies heavily on Storyteller fiat. That's largely necessary because of how open Mage is.<br /> <br /> To clarify: I don't come up with system hacks to make the game playable; I come up with system hacks to fine-tune the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-10-2021, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T14:35:01-07:00","id":1448167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448145#post1448145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I formulated the post in the form of a question. The idea is to clarify some things I am having trouble with.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's difficult to try to help with clarity when the questions feel so out of step with the topic that you can't figure out what you're trying to clarify.<br /> <br /> If someone asked you, &quot;why is the cover of Mage this horrible puke green color?&quot; while you're sitting there looking at the very clearly purple cover of the book, I'm assuming you would have some serious confusion about the situation at hand. That's how some of your questions made me feel in terms of confusion about what you were even asking about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I thought that when Paradox comes to repair reality, it blurs Sleepers' memories. </div> </div> </div>Paradox doesn't &quot;repair&quot; reality. As much as reality is being repaired, Paradox is an energetic reaction to harming it in the first place.<br /> <br /> To go to a common analogy, Paradox is reality's white blood cells. When you get a cut on your finger, your white blood cells aren't sent to the injury to fix anything, they're there to attack anything that doesn't belong. The scary part of this analogy is that the microbes your immune system is trying to destroy are capable of summoning something to cut your skin open so they can get inside you instead of having to hang around waiting for a cut to happen on its own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it is mainly NWO Operatives having to run around editing the memory of every Sleeper who witnessed something, the Traditions *would* want to leave lasting memories of Vulgar Magick. </div> </div> </div>This is quite an exaggeration of what I said. Mages don't need to mind wipe every witness, because most witnesses will either rationalize it in a harmless (to mages) fashion, or be such unreliable witnesses to other humans that people will just treat them as crazy (probably until they start doubting reality to an unhealthy degree).<br /> <br /> The Technocracy tolerates a lot of wacko conspiracy theories because they're great at scooping up Sleeper witnesses to vulgar magic and rendering them harmless to the Union's goals. Consider that in the WoD, it is very likely that most ufologists, big foot researchers, and ghost hunters are people that saw real supernatural events (Awakened magic or something else, doesn't really matter) and are desperate to prove that what they saw was real to a world that didn't believe a word of it. They end up beneficial to the Technocracy because the majority of people see them as quacks who are fun to laugh at on reality TV shows, and they tend to get into other conspiracies, such as the Men In Black, that the Technocracy can leverage to exercise even more control over society.<br /> <br /> The Traditions also have laws against excessive use of vulgar magic in front of Sleepers, and carelessly dragging individual Sleepers into the politics and battles of Awakened magic. Some of this is a level of ethical standards that makes the Traditions protagonist material, and some of it is good old self-preservation. The Technocracy are not the only witch-hunters in the WoD. Lots of things in the WoD would kill a mage if the chance presented itself, so casting big flashy magic that leaves lots of witnesses is just telling all those enemies where you are.<br /> <br /> There are mages that try what you're thinking of (namely the Taftani), it's not going super great for them (but better than most Tradition mages would like to acknowledge).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As long as the Operatives are occupied with a constant massive cover up, they have way less time to spy on and assassinate Tradition Mages. It is worth the cost in terms of a few points of Paradox to produce an event that forces Blacksuits to show up at a specific location and repeatedly Mindwipe people. I do not see how the Technocracy could function without Paradox acting on the memories of witnesses. </div> </div> </div>The Union is an organization with significantly more resources than the Traditions, and have an easier time operating in Consensus. They have clean up crews and wetwork teams operating as separate units. If the Traditions spent all their time casting Vulgar magic with Witnesses, they'd have no defenses during all the downtime bleeding off Paradox, and they'd be that much easier to wipe out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448146#post1448146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can build your character to avoid the consequences with Arcane, Familiar and Prime to cloak your Resonance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arcane does not help you if you run around doing obvious things.... like casting blatant Vulgar magic in public. Familiars are also thinking feeling beings that do not want to be your Paradox sponge. Abusing Familiars can have nasty consequences.<br /> <br /> Yes, you can build your character to minimize the direct consequences of Paradox, but it doesn't mean you can eliminate consequences.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448148#post1448148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I get from this is that the game I love is totally absurd, rules wise.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing absurd about a rule just because it enforces a different game-state reality than you'd like.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448150#post1448150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where, in Ascension, is the incentive to slowly use coincidental effects to change the Consensus?</div> </div> </div> </div>Magic, fundamentally, isn't how you change Consensus. Consensus is about what people believe, and people believe things without mages using magic to make them believe things. <br /> <br /> As Dataweaver pointed out, the two are separate considerations. You do coincidental magic because it's better for you in the long run, and you want to change Consensus because its better for you in the long run. You combine them because they're both long term considerations for how to best go about achieving your goals, not because there is a direct link between them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448155#post1448155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some kind of hack is required to make Ascension playable. I would be curious to know what percentage storytellers use RAW and if homebrew adaptations all attempt to address a common set of inconsistencies between the rules and the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've play Ascension with out hacks just fine. Most of my house rules aren't even about the magic side of the game, but about the mundane side of the game. And like Dataweaver they're changes I make to make the game fit what I want better, not because the game is unplayable if you don't to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T18:16:36-07:00","id":1448181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448167#post1448167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's difficult to try to help with clarity when the questions feel so out of step with the topic that you can't figure out what you're trying to clarify.</div> </div> </div> </div>People responded, adding their own ideas. The conversation evolved in a particular direction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448167#post1448167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If someone asked you, &quot;why is the cover of Mage this horrible puke green color?&quot; while you're sitting there looking at the very clearly purple cover of the book, I'm assuming you would have some serious confusion about the situation at hand. That's how some of your questions made me feel in terms of confusion about what you were even asking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is all about how you run the simulation of these rules in your mind, I guess. <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448167#post1448167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paradox doesn't &quot;repair&quot; reality. As much as reality is being repaired, Paradox is an energetic reaction to harming it in the first place.<br /> <br /> To go to a common analogy, Paradox is reality's white blood cells. When you get a cut on your finger, your white blood cells aren't sent to the injury to fix anything, they're there to attack anything that doesn't belong. The scary part of this analogy is that the microbes your immune system is trying to destroy are capable of summoning something to cut your skin open so they can get inside you instead of having to hang around waiting for a cut to happen on its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Sleeper exists in, is part of and helps shape the local Reality Zone with his belief. In the case of many Sleepers dying of a Magickal Effect, does that influence how the white blood cells of Paradox respond, if someone is trying to save them? It's not so much about Paradox having moral judgement as selectively targeting the Mage causing the damage rather than the Mage trying to counteract or heal the injury. <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448167#post1448167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is quite an exaggeration of what I said. Mages don't need to mind wipe every witness, because most witnesses will either rationalize it in a harmless (to mages) fashion, or be such unreliable witnesses to other humans that people will just treat them as crazy (probably until they start doubting reality to an unhealthy degree).<br /> <br /> The Technocracy tolerates a lot of wacko conspiracy theories because they're great at scooping up Sleeper witnesses to vulgar magic and rendering them harmless to the Union's goals. Consider that in the WoD, it is very likely that most ufologists, big foot researchers, and ghost hunters are people that saw real supernatural events (Awakened magic or something else, doesn't really matter) and are desperate to prove that what they saw was real to a world that didn't believe a word of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>If a whole bunch of Sleepers witness the same event in the same place, they can establish communication with each other, exchanging telephone numbers. They would not be lone individuals with nobody else to support their account of what happened.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448167#post1448167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Traditions also have laws against excessive use of vulgar magic in front of Sleepers, and carelessly dragging individual Sleepers into the politics and battles of Awakened magic. Some of this is a level of ethical standards that makes the Traditions protagonist material, and some of it is good old self-preservation. The Technocracy are not the only witch-hunters in the WoD. Lots of things in the WoD would kill a mage if the chance presented itself, so casting big flashy magic that leaves lots of witnesses is just telling all those enemies where you are.</div> </div> </div> </div>It only signals that you were within line of site of the place where the effect went off. Depending on your vantage point, line of sight can be quite far. Correspondence further extends that. There is time to get away or change positions before most things can show up.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448167#post1448167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are mages that try what you're thinking of (namely the Taftani), it's not going super great for them (but better than most Tradition mages would like to acknowledge).<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Union is an organization with significantly more resources than the Traditions, and have an easier time operating in Consensus. They have clean up crews and wetwork teams operating as separate units. If the Traditions spent all their time casting Vulgar magic with Witnesses, they'd have no defenses during all the downtime bleeding off Paradox, and they'd be that much easier to wipe out.</div> </div> </div> </div>How is it that the Technocracy does not use its vast army to wipe out the Taftani? If they are using Vulgar Magick, do they not have to lay around bleeding off Paradox.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448167#post1448167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, you can build your character to minimize the direct consequences of Paradox, but it doesn't mean you can eliminate consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>Minimizing is fine. Two dice of bashing damage, your hair sparkles, whatever.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448167#post1448167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's nothing absurd about a rule just because it enforces a different game-state reality than you'd like.</div> </div> </div> </div>It enforces a game state where the Consensus would unravel into Marauder-Village fast enough. <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448167#post1448167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magic, fundamentally, isn't how you change Consensus. Consensus is about what people believe, and people believe things without mages using magic to make them believe things.</div> </div> </div> </div>The speaker at a TED conference whose voice is enhanced with a Life + Forces + Mind effect is going to convince more people. Effect enhancing Ability.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448167#post1448167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Dataweaver pointed out, the two are separate considerations. You do coincidental magic because it's better for you in the long run, and you want to change Consensus because its better for you in the long run. You combine them because they're both long term considerations for how to best go about achieving your goals, not because there is a direct link between them.</div> </div> </div> </div>All three of us seem to prefer a game where subtlety and diligence by players is rewarded. The difference for me is that when I run the simulation of a blatant Vulgar Effect in my mind, I get a different aftermath.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-10T19:44:01-07:00","id":1448188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448181#post1448181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is all about how you run the simulation of these rules in your mind, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of a simulation, you get different results from different inputs. If you've run a lot of variants of a simulation, you usually get a sense of what inputs are going in. I'm struggling with that second part.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the case of many Sleepers dying of a Magickal Effect, does that influence how the white blood cells of Paradox respond, if someone is trying to save them? It's not so much about Paradox having moral judgement as selectively targeting the Mage causing the damage rather than the Mage trying to counteract or heal the injury. </div> </div> </div>In a small way, Paradox does care, but it really comes down to the kind of Quiets that the mage gets smacked with. Basically, Paradox does react to the Resonance of magic when it responds, but it is still indiscriminate. <br /> <br /> Paradox doesn't respond to intent.<br /> <br /> I'm going to spoiler tag this for medical squick:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">So to keep to the injury thing.<br /> <br /> The murderous mage does a lot of horrible damage, the wound is nasty and infected, and all that.<br /> <br /> The healing mage knows that the wound can't heal that damage by itself. So they toss in medical maggots. They eat up all the badly damaged flesh, that's good!<br /> <br /> But, to Paradox, the white blood cells just see intruders. The response to nasty bacteria and parasites might not be identical, but the white blood cells can't tell the difference enough not to attack. The bacteria set off a Jhor reaction, and the maggots a Clarity reaction, but a reaction has to happen.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a whole bunch of Sleepers witness the same event in the same place, they can establish communication with each other, exchanging telephone numbers. They would not be lone individuals with nobody else to support their account of what happened. </div> </div> </div>It's a possibility, but that's why the Technocracy keeps around agents to mind wipe people if they can't control them with less overt measures. They don't start with mindwipes unless the incident was really drastic. They start with being in with the cops that show up to interview everyone and take down identifying information about the witnesses, then they're in with the NSA to spy on those individuals to see if they're moving on or not, etc. <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It only signals that you were within line of site of the place where the effect went off. Depending on your vantage point, line of sight can be quite far. Correspondence further extends that. There is time to get away or change positions before most things can show up. </div> </div> </div>And lots of things in the WoD can follow the trail of magical energy around. The point isn't that you can't get away with it at all, but you can't get away with it too many times.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How is it that the Technocracy does not use its vast army to wipe out the Taftani? If they are using Vulgar Magick, do they not have to lay around bleeding off Paradox. </div> </div> </div>The Syndicate doesn't want to waste the resources trying to invade the rather large Reality Zone the Taftani have been maintaining in the Arabian desert. They have the Taftani surrounded and contained, and are happy to slowly eat away at their territory. And again, the Union uses non-mage assets first. They're stoking sectarian violence, and Islamic persecution of pre-Islamic faiths (aka the Sleepers the Taftani draw from) so Sleepers do most of the work; plus getting OPEC leaders further into their pockets by making them reliant on foreign military resources.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Minimizing is fine. Two dice of bashing damage, your hair sparkles, whatever. </div> </div> </div>And that's why the ST gets to say when Paradox goes off, so it can build up and you face worse than that.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It enforces a game state where the Consensus would unravel into Marauder-Village fast enough. </div> </div> </div>You haven't really established this. There are 8 billion people on Earth. How does a few dozen seeing true magic in action even start to dent Consensus?<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The speaker at a TED conference whose voice is enhanced with a Life + Forces + Mind effect is going to convince more people. Effect enhancing Ability. </div> </div> </div>You hardly need that many Spheres.<br /> <br /> Also yeah, the Technocracy loves TED talks to further spread their control. You think the Traditions are the ones on there? TED is a wonderful way the Union to continue their efforts to keep Consensus how they like it.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All three of us seem to prefer a game where subtlety and diligence by players is rewarded. The difference for me is that when I run the simulation of a blatant Vulgar Effect in my mind, I get a different aftermath. </div> </div> </div>And I continue to be unsure of why you get those results from the game-as-written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T11:53:36-07:00","id":1448246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448188#post1448188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of a simulation, you get different results from different inputs. If you've run a lot of variants of a simulation, you usually get a sense of what inputs are going in. I'm struggling with that second part.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448188#post1448188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You haven't really established this. There are 8 billion people on Earth. How does a few dozen seeing true magic in action even start to dent Consensus?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mage who wants to have the greatest effect on the Consensus for the lowest cost to himself will create the effect at a large public event that will be witnessed by Thousands of people. He only has to do this once to have a serious impact. Using RAW, he can do this and get away at least once. <br /> <br /> The astonishment on the faces of everyone confirms that everyone has seen something totally out of the ordinary and the witnesses will start confirming this with each other. They are now a group, not isolated individuals. The internal psychological mechanism that causes someone to rationalize is counteracted by the group of people who are wanting to communicate with each other about what just happened. <br /> <br /> Try adding a freshly made character whose Spheres, Abilities, Attributes, Backgrounds and Merits are tailored for this purpose. If that's not sufficient, tack on and allocate XP until they can do something spectacular. Imagine it is an NPC antagonist and the players are noble Technomancers trying to prevent this recent event from impacting the Consensus.<br /> <br /> &quot;It feels&quot; almost as if you are determined to find fault with what I post. I am down to considering posting a scene-by-scene-RAW to defend my ability to say something. \u200b<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T12:25:00-07:00","id":1448253,"title":"","content":"I'm not trying to make you feel defensive here. But my issue is that assertion that the greatest impact for the lowest cost is big flashy magic because.... it's not.<br /> <br /> Taking the concept of &quot;thousands&quot; to its most generous extremes means impacting less than 0.01% of Sleepers. How is that going to radically alter Consensus in the face of the unaffected 99.99%, even before the Technocracy absolutely steps in to mitigate most of the impact it would have on the thousands (keeping in mind they're just as if not more capable of influencing Sleepers on mass, and they can do so coincidentally, so they'll more easily overpower anything done).<br /> <br /> You brought up TED talks, which I feel are very much NWO and Syndicate approved, but if you want to influence Sleepers? YouTube and similar social media have proven themselves to be able to let you reach millions of people that are willing to get into ideas that oppose the Union's end goals (though they don't necessarily support the Tradition's end goals either). No Tradition mage wants to spread QAnon BS, but they'd love to replicate that sort of cultural impact with their own messages.<br /> <br /> That's why I don't see the whole &quot;do big flash magic once&quot; idea the same as you. I don't see how the cost/benefit plays out how you're thinking because the numbers just don't seem to be there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T15:34:30-07:00","id":1448265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448253#post1448253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not trying to make you feel defensive here. But my issue is that assertion that the greatest impact for the lowest cost is big flashy magic because.... it's not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe. Here, I am referring to a Mage who choses this tactic, plans for maximum impact and then simulating the results.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448253#post1448253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taking the concept of &quot;thousands&quot; to its most generous extremes means impacting less than 0.01% of Sleepers. How is that going to radically alter Consensus in the face of the unaffected 99.99%,</div> </div> </div> </div>Information spreads instantaneously over the internet, once someone uploads. A thousand people, most of who have cell phones are going to communicate to the rest of the world. The 99.99% have phones and computers too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448253#post1448253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">even before the Technocracy absolutely steps in to mitigate most of the impact it would have on the thousands (keeping in mind they're just as if not more capable of influencing Sleepers on mass, and they can do so coincidentally, so they'll more easily overpower anything done).</div> </div> </div> </div>Suppose the Virtual Adapts assist the group in getting around the technocracy's filters, which they are practiced at doing. There is also the simple tactic of documenting the cover-up, the mundane aspects that can be caught on camera, since you can plan in advance of the Technocracy's unenlightened assets showing up. <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448253#post1448253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You brought up TED talks, which I feel are very much NWO and Syndicate approved, but if you want to influence Sleepers? YouTube and similar social media have proven themselves to be able to let you reach millions of people that are willing to get into ideas that oppose the Union's end goals (though they don't necessarily support the Tradition's end goals either). No Tradition mage wants to spread QAnon BS, but they'd love to replicate that sort of cultural impact with their own messages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Extinction Rebellion are a very small group, by membership in any one country, but manage to force the issue of climate change into discussions between billionaires at Davos and keep it in public consciousness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T16:19:01-07:00","id":1448266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448265#post1448265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe. Here, I am referring to a Mage who choses this tactic, plans for maximum impact and then simulating the results.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that, effectively, you're assuming this mage perfectly achieves everything, and everyone opposed to his plan fails at all attempts to stop them. Again, the Technocracy aren't the only potential obstacles here. What are the plans for a Euthanatos sniper, who's already aware of the goal through divination, that's waiting to pull the trigger the moment before the mage can cast their grand effect? The Chakravanti are one of the Traditions that would absolutely leave the Traditions if they abandoned the Rule of Shade, and have no compunction about stopping mages that go rogue and dealing with the backlash later.<br /> <br /> It's not really running the simulation if you give one side cheat codes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Information spreads instantaneously over the internet, once someone uploads. </div> </div> </div>Information isn't belief. Once it's digital, once you aren't there to see it, you can say, &quot;wow, that's great special effects, who afforded hiring so many extras? Or did they dupe all these people somehow?&quot; The Internet is a mess of real and fake, and everyone know it. Anything that belies belief is quickly dismissed as fake (even if it isn't).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Suppose the Virtual Adapts assist the group in getting around the technocracy's filters, which they are practiced at doing. There is also the simple tactic of documenting the cover-up, the mundane aspects that can be caught on camera, since you can plan in advance of the Technocracy's unenlightened assets showing up. </div> </div> </div>Why are the VAs giving a shit about this? Why are the Technocrats being treated as only having a few layers of reaction when they're stated to have dozens?<br /> <br /> \u200bThis is the kind of stuff that goes into &quot;cheat codes invalidate this run of the simulate.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Technocracy, when pushed, covered up <b>nuking a city in India and killing millions of civilians, and then firing a space laser when nukes didn't work</b> in response to a superpowered vampire waking up. That was a huge expenditure on their part, they can't do that every day or probably more than once or twice a year at best, but that's the cover up machine we're talking about here.<br /> <br /> The VAs, like most online underground groups, know that part of their ability to get away with what they get away with, is to never press things too hard and provoke too big of a response. Because part of the skill of getting away with stuff online is not making yourself the biggest problem for the people trying to control things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Extinction Rebellion are a very small group, by membership in any one country, but manage to force the issue of climate change into discussions between billionaires at Davos and keep it in public consciousness. </div> </div> </div>First... that's kind of proving my point. Extinction Rebellion doesn't need magic to do that. They're waging an influence campaign with just normal human influence tactics adapted to the times.<br /> <br /> Second, part of their success is that they are far from the only group of climate change activists, let alone general population that thinks something should be done about climate change. They're working on something that is, in Mage terms, part of the Consensus already, not trying to get people to believe something like you can learn to throw fireballs with your mind.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T18:48:34-07:00","id":1448281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448266#post1448266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that, effectively, you're assuming this mage perfectly achieves everything, and everyone opposed to his plan fails at all attempts to stop them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am saying the game mechanics allow this Mage to do this with a great number of successes before anyone knows he is going to do it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448266#post1448266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a Euthanatos sniper, who's already aware of the goal through divination, that's waiting to pull the trigger the moment before the mage can cast their grand effect?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448266#post1448266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not really running the simulation if you give one side cheat codes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that you should not give one side cheat codes. You have given the &quot;Your Idea Sucks&quot; team a Euthanatos sniper who showed up in advance and now we have to get into the limits of Time 2 Magick to predict events. Or not. <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448266#post1448266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are the VAs giving a shit about this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because, they are opposed to the Technocracy stopping the free flow of information. It is kind of what they are all about, having defected over this issue. There is at least one subgroup of the VAs who want to spread chaos (not violence) in a way that undermines the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448266#post1448266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are the Technocrats being treated as only having a few layers of reaction when they're stated to have dozens?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Reaction&quot; is the key word. They show up in vehicles. They have to hear about the event and then show up. It could be a twenty minute drive. A lot can happen in twenty minutes.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448266#post1448266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the kind of stuff that goes into &quot;cheat codes invalidate this run of the simulate.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly, a Euthanatos hit man should not show up in advance every time a player or NPC tries to do something. <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448266#post1448266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Technocracy, when pushed, covered up <b>nuking a city in India and killing millions of civilians, and then firing a space laser when nukes didn't work</b> in response to a superpowered vampire waking up. That was a huge expenditure on their part, they can't do that every day or probably more than once or twice a year at best, but that's the cover up machine we're talking about here.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Technocracy is Superman, but evil. They are waiting around every corner.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448266#post1448266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The VAs, like most online underground groups, know that part of their ability to get away with what they get away with, is to never press things too hard and provoke too big of a response. Because part of the skill of getting away with stuff online is not making yourself the biggest problem for the people trying to control things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all. Some VAs want to challenge the Technocracy on the digital front, taking risks to cause impact.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448266#post1448266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First... that's kind of proving my point. Extinction Rebellion doesn't need magic to do that. They're waging an influence campaign with just normal human influence tactics adapted to the times.<br /> <br /> Second, part of their success is that they are far from the only group of climate change activists, let alone general population that thinks something should be done about climate change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since the Technocracy is all-powerful and omnipresent in the setting, climate change should be fixed already. It is in their interest to solve it.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448266#post1448266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're working on something that is, in Mage terms, part of the Consensus already, not trying to get people to believe something like you can learn to throw fireballs with your mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. The Mage in the simulation, before being sniped by the precognizant hit man, was planning to use Vulgar Magic to change the Consensus. Now we can simulate a parade of Technomancer NPCs marching over the corpse of my poor dude with a banner that says, &quot;The Rules as Written are perfect and the Technocracy always wins.&quot;. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T19:32:02-07:00","id":1448285,"title":"","content":"This is getting pointlessly hostile.<br /> <br /> You have a character that is actively seeking help from other mages, but object to the idea that some of those other mages might use their own abilities to stop them. It's not a secret at some point, even if other mages that want to stop it are going to have to work to find out enough details to interfere.<br /> <br /> I presented the canon extent of the Technocracy's abilities in covering things up, acknowledged it's an extreme that they can't keep doing, but to point out what their maximum effort looks like, and you're ignoring that limitation to make it sound like I'm calling them omnipotent.<br /> <br /> If you want to take another swing at this that's aimed at actually talking this out, I'd love to have that conversation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T23:49:14-07:00","id":1448302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448285#post1448285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I presented the canon extent of the Technocracy's abilities in covering things up (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think rather than covering them up, the Technocracy be default would deal with such problems by going all Minority Report on them. A Time 2 Correspondence 3 Prime 1 Procedure would detect extremely Vulgar uses of Magick which threaten the Consensus, before they occur. There is even a Methodology just for the job - the NWO Watchers (and maybe also the Ivory Tower).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T01:21:23-07:00","id":1448303,"title":"","content":"I think you might need better Spheres, or at least a crapton of successes to scan the whole world and an indefinite amount of time into the future for an unknown person or event. Which is a lot even for the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> They invest in more mundane intelligence gathering for a reason. If one of their agents overhears some troubling talk at The Spy's Demise? Then that sort of divinatory scrying makes more sense once they can get even some minor details like a name, a place, a time, or whatnot to help narrow down their search to something manageable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T05:35:11-07:00","id":1448315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448303#post1448303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think you might need better Spheres, or at least a crapton of successes to scan the whole world and an indefinite amount of time into the future for an unknown person or event. Which is a lot even for the Technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recall that some newly Awakened Mages are swiftly found by Mage groups, so there is this capability of general scanning 'into the unknown' for distinct phenomena and persons. I think that especially rare events might be somehow relatively easy to track; consider that because of their uniqueness, they make an impression on the Tapestry.<br /> Better Spheres are needed indeed. Time 3 or 4 cause it is a non-specific event. Prime 4 or 5 to detect Paradox and/or potential Consensus shifting. The time period scanned might actually be specified, and the Procedure simply repeated regularly. Likewise, a single use of such a Procedure does not need to target the whole world - areas of the world can be designated and multiple (quite many, I think) instances of the Procedure could then be executed. Practically uninhabited areas can be ignored in the scanning. It's still a lot of work, but I'm thinking it's just the kind of Procedure the New World Order (and other Technocrats, perhaps) would devote time and effort towards.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448303#post1448303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They invest in more mundane intelligence gathering for a reason. If one of their agents overhears some troubling talk at The Spy's Demise? Then that sort of divinatory scrying makes more sense once they can get even some minor details like a name, a place, a time, or whatnot to help narrow down their search to something manageable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course. Technocrats could run Enlightened psychological, sociological, and statistical analysis (as Procedures, most likely) on groups of Mages to identify individuals most likely to do this kind of secrecy and Consensus breaking action. Then they try to ascertain when, how, and where it might happen - through Procedures or mundane analysis (if any such analysis could be called mundane).<br /> <br /> (What's Spy's Demise ?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 05-12-2021, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T11:35:32-07:00","id":1448340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448285#post1448285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is getting pointlessly hostile.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have not posted in some months. I forgot to expect what happens every time I post anything that touches on RAW. There is someone Pointing at me saying, &quot;This guy doesn't know shit. He thinks the book cover is puke-green because he's full of assumptions.&quot;. There is a social aspect of posting. I like talking to other people who play and run Mage games, which are mostly on pause for the forever-lockdown. <br /> <br /> I was just speaking, in person, to a GM who runs games for very large groups of people. He was saying that for every game system that he has ever played or run, there had to be changes to the rules to make the game function and everyone approved of the changes. It is ASSUMED that you will have to do this. <br /> <br /> In Ascension, the alternative is jack up the Technocracy with so much Hypertech Steroids and overactive cloning vats that you can put them everywhere. It makes for a lot of generic goons. Eventually, I am going to do a post on how a &quot;thinner&quot; Technocracy is more fun for players and easier for the storyteller (at least in my case) to hold in his head. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448285#post1448285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to take another swing at this that's aimed at actually talking this out, I'd love to have that conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. We need a fresh idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448315#post1448315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Better Spheres are needed indeed. Time 3 or 4 cause it is a non-specific event. Prime 4 or 5 to detect Paradox and/or potential Consensus shifting. The time period scanned might actually be specified, and the Procedure simply repeated regularly. Likewise, a single use of such a Procedure does not need to target the whole world - areas of the world can be designated and multiple (quite many, I think) instances of the Procedure could then be executed. It's still a lot of work, but I'm thinking it's just the kind of Procedure the New World Order (and other Technocrats, perhaps) would devote time and effort towards.</div> </div> </div> </div>This gives me an idea. The goal, for me, is to have something (I used the ever-present force of Paradox) erase memory. Let's suppose a group of Technomancers have the time, luxury and believing Sleeper participants to do a Conjunctional Magick Ritual to erase the memory of witnesses to Vulgar Magick within a long range of the place the ritual was done. I will go through the effect, Sphere by Sphere.<br /> <br /> Time 4 Triggered Effect: The effect will be activated under certain conditions.<br /> <br /> Prime, at the level needed to detect Paradox, combined with Mind 2 and Entropy 1 to detect the number of witnesses. The effect only goes off if there are many witnesses.<br /> <br /> Correspondence 3 to extend the range of detection, as well as the range of delivery of the effect.<br /> <br /> Mind 4 is the main effect. Erasing or editing the memories of the witnesses. Correspondence also extends the area of effect. <br /> <br /> Forces 3 could be added to make the effect more coincidental and believable for the Technomancers doing the casting. The explanation is that a satellite is sending the instructions to the brains of the targets via microwave signal. Add life 3 to specifically target the brain. <br /> <br /> Story-wise, this is less punitive than having goons show up out of nowhere every time the players try to do something and it maintains the consistency of the Consensus. The players realize they have not achieved anything by their flagrant use of Vulgar Magick and they know the goons will start to look for them. Time to retreat, cover their tracks and plan a more subtle method for changing the Consensus.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T11:48:01-07:00","id":1448342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448315#post1448315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recall that some newly Awakened Mages are swiftly found by Mage groups, so there is this capability of general scanning 'into the unknown' for distinct phenomena and persons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always read this as mostly because newly Awakened mages do things that make them easy to find because they don't know better: cast magic that causes a minor stir, start hitting up every rare book shop and new age store looking for information on what happened, etc. You also have groups like the Akashayana and Chakravanti that track Avatars through incarnations, and use that to focus divinations on who to watch for Awakenings rather than purely looking for the unknown.<br /> <br /> It just seems to me, and informed by books like Initiates of the Arts (however out of date that might be now), that the mudan-ish effort to get enough details to make the magical part of tracking people down is worth it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (What's Spy's Demise ?) </div> </div> </div>A &quot;bar&quot; in the Digital Web that's the primary &quot;neutral ground&quot; of the virtual world. Anyone that has the skills to find it, and abides by the rules, is allowed in; making it a hub of information trading, spying, and intrigue. It's one of the few places the Traditions and Technocracy can exchange information without worrying about the meeting being a trap (the information being a trap is a separate matter); such as passing on information about where a Nephandi threat might be.<br /> <br /> The name is a reference to an early 80s video game, but it's also supposed to evoke the film Casablanca.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T12:29:59-07:00","id":1448349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448340#post1448340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a social aspect of posting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I kept reiterating my confusion. If I can't tell if a thread is, &quot;What if....[insert alteration to the rules or setting&quot; or if the thread is, &quot;Is this really [insert rules or setting]&quot; it's hard for me to know what sort of social engagement to offer up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was just speaking, in person, to a GM who runs games for very large groups of people. He was saying that for every game system that he has ever played or run, there had to be changes to the rules to make the game function and everyone approved of the changes. It is ASSUMED that you will have to do this. </div> </div> </div>That is, however, on opinion. A common one that GM is hardly unique in having of course, but not a universal one.<br /> <br /> A lot of people feel the most RPGs, or at least one of the benchmarks for a good RPG, is that rules should be flexible enough to handle the variations of different gaming groups as long as the group has bought into the premise of the game. From the perspective, a game where people feel they have to change the rules is a poorly designed game (or at least a poorly designed part of the game). People might want to change the rules, because lots of valid reasons, but the game should still work even if they don't.<br /> <br /> People absolutely should change the rules if it will make the game more fun for their group, but assuming you have to, to me, just feels like you're never giving the RAW a fair shot to see if the results are fun as written.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In Ascension, the alternative is jack up the Technocracy with so much Hypertech Steroids and overactive cloning vats that you can put them everywhere. </div> </div> </div>What is this the alternative to though?<br /> <br /> You seem very resistant to the idea that there are plenty of mages, and non-mages, out there that don't want people running around casting blatant vulgar magic in front of a bunch of Sleepers. Or what if the people that help and encourage such actions turn out to be Nephandi or Marauders?<br /> <br /> You seem to be making a fairly large excluded middle where either it &quot;has&quot; to be that a single dedicated mage can rip apart Consensus with a few well placed Vulgar castings, or the Technocracy has to be exaggerated to the extreme.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Forces 3 could be added to make the effect more coincidental and believable for the Technomancers doing the casting. The explanation is that a satellite is sending the instructions to the brains of the targets via microwave signal. Add life 3 to specifically target the brain. </div> </div> </div>That seems fairly unnecessary. The satellites are part of the instruments of the effect, you don't need Forces to make them part of it to keep things coincidental (not sure how the do that though). Mind doesn't need Life to &quot;target the brain.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Story-wise, this is less punitive than having goons show up out of nowhere every time the players try to do something and it maintains the consistency of the Consensus. The players realize they have not achieved anything by their flagrant use of Vulgar Magick and they know the goons will start to look for them. Time to retreat, cover their tracks and plan a more subtle method for changing the Consensus.<br /> </div> </div> </div>And.... now I'm back to confused. Both cases come down to the thing that influences players, is that Union goons show up because they're not being subtle enough after the Technocrats use their power to undo the impact of the Vulgar magic on the general populace. All I can see is that you spelled out a potential rote that the Union might use for what I was talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-12T19:09:12-07:00","id":1448376,"title":"","content":"If you want to hack the game so that Sleepers forget any Vulgar Magick they witness, I strongly reiterate my suggestion to get the Mage Translation Guide and Mage the Awakening, and port over its memory-loss mechanism. I don't find it necessary in my games; but if it helps you with yours, go for it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T06:21:35-07:00","id":1448413,"title":"","content":"Of course its possible that a suitably powerful and appropriately specced mage might try and do something horribly vulgar in front of a massive crowd to influence the masses and thereby change the consensus. You could build a campaign around this as either technocracy (trying to stop them) or traditions/crafts (trying to stop them/trying to help them).<br /> The assumptions we make going forward depend ENTIRELY on the game you are playing. No NPC does this. Its simply too dangerous, difficult, fatal.<br /> If you want to stop it then give the rebel mage allies, have him be very powerful (high arete so he can actually pull it off), even have it happen, then the PCs have to handle clean up. If people see something very flashy then maybe the PCs need to run point on launching hologram technology into the consensus a decade early and control the narrative that it was a public entertainment test. If it was something dangerous where lots of people died then maybe it was a bomb and hallucinagenic gas launch, and they have to scrub the digital traces, track down and neuralzye key communicators, etc.<br /> If the PCs want to be the ones to do it then you'll need to throw all sorts of creative traps and hurdles at them. How do they manage to do it, (high difficulty, high numbers of success, high paradox). How do they escape the wrath of the traditions AND the technocracy. What else crawls out the woordwork afterwards? Vampires/Garou/Ghosts, depending on WHAT they do to achieve this mass vulgar event, any other group might also show up. How do they spread the message even further, how to they work against the technocracy cover up attempt.<br /> <br /> All this &quot;It wouldn't work&quot; &quot;It would work&quot; discussion is pointless. The setting isn't telling a story, it is the setting for YOUR story. Tell us how it worked in your game or how your players stopped it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4249-gribblethemunchkin","name":"gribblethemunchkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T15:00:59-07:00","id":1448470,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Please don't say previous discussion is pointless.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-13T16:35:51-07:00","id":1448476,"title":"","content":"Agreeing with most of what was said above, that the setting *can* be broken it's not necessarily a bad thing. If it <i>couldn't</i> be broken, then the Traditions and other faction's figth it's for naugh.<br /> <br /> What does matter, I think, it's if it it makes sense for the setting to have survived<i> 'til now</i>. It's only fair to consider how this plan could have failed, and why. It would be a bad thing if it was so <i>easy</i>, that someone should already have done it. Or if it was such a good method that trully being subtle seems dumb.<br /> <br /> But precisely because these kind of plans have a lot of moving parts and opposing forces, I think it's reasonable to think it's not that easy, and it - not being <i>impossible</i> - just <i>failed </i>up until now.<br /> <br /> The Taftani aproved the plan, tried it, and got mix results: They're too small a faction to change the world - but, HEY, they managed to keep their ugly desertic Reality Zone. It's not like the Technocracy didn't <i>tried </i>to wipe them out entirely, but the Craft managed to make it <i>too expensive </i>to bother - Technocracy was like: &quot;who wants that desert anyway?, keep it!&quot; - For the time being, of course, because the Technocracy it's in a very complex war against multiple forces.<br /> <br /> M20 goes with the Taftani have starting to favor subtler methods, to infiltrate the modern world and expand their influence beyond their small place - I don't like it, but it is what it is<br /> <br /> The Traditions are much more powerful than the Taftani, but also have a lot of organizational problems. Some mages would be opposed to break the Rule of Shade for moral reasons and others because they don't want to eat 'dox for &quot;the cause&quot;, while surely others would figth for what Paradigm get's more camera time (or just use the whole thing to throw political rivals under the bus, <i>any</i> bus) ... I say this to showcase how convincing them to go for it would be a political feat of no small magnitude (and prob. the kind of thing that takes decades of blood and tears, with no small amount of assassination attempts) - and that's just to start the plan with some backing<br /> <br /> If you don't get a faction behind and do it as a rogue or a band of rogues...well. I see a problem if the Technocracy it's so strong that they can just obliterate the Traditions, but I see not so much of a problem with them being able to overpower a loner. I hope you have some serious personal power and a realy good plan...<br /> <br /> And you really should account for things like future sigth (Nephandi and other vile mages do that - they obscure their personal timelines so often, some mages would become suspicious of you if they can't see your future. You should, at least, be <i>that</i> careful. Probably more, I would ask the ST if I can add Mind to project<i> a fake future</i> to those that would try to peek) <hr /><br /> While Paradox doesn't erase memory (and doesn't care much about the number of people). There's at least one case I can think of where Paradox was so big, it <i>could</i> have had the secondary effect of erasing the memory of a fact: rogue archmaster Czar Vargo's case.<br /> <br /> That case it's interesting, because in some books it was stated that the Technocracy defeated Vargo and then erased the memory of everyone in the biggest cities of the world. But if my memory doesn't fail, in Revised it's suggested that the Technocracy wishes they had that kind of power, that Paradox erased Vargo's fleet from reality and it was like it never happened. People forgot that time when a crazy scientist almost takes over the world...<br /> <br /> Let's note that this wasn't Paradox affecting the mind of Sleepers, but rather a fact being <i>erased from reality</i> affecting the memory of sleepers.<br /> <br /> I happened after a Vulgar fight against the Technocracy, that probably accumulated quite an amount of 'dox in separate instances. It would be a break from the normal rules ... unless, perhaps, Wrinkle was involved (as erasing someone from time does cause the secondary effect of having people forget...since the erased never existed)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-13-2021, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T10:53:47-07:00","id":1449012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1447854-save-a-sleeper-with-vulgar-magick?p=1448342#post1448342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always read this as mostly because newly Awakened mages do things that make them easy to find because they don't know better: cast magic that causes a minor stir, start hitting up every rare book shop and new age store looking for information on what happened, etc. You also have groups like the Akashayana and Chakravanti that track Avatars through incarnations, and use that to focus divinations on who to watch for Awakenings rather than purely looking for the unknown.<br /> <br /> It just seems to me, and informed by books like Initiates of the Arts (however out of date that might be now), that the mudan-ish effort to get enough details to make the magical part of tracking people down is worth it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This works as well, though I prefer the idea of powerful divinations and scrying locating new Mages. It seems more cohesive than relying on favorable circumstances.<br /> In regard to tracking Awakenings, I found this is Void Engineers Revised CB, in description of one of the example characters (Parabiologist, p. 102) :<br /> &quot;You staggered out of the cave system into the light - and the arms of a Void Engineer rescue team. They'd detected a flare of Primal Energy from your location: the residue of your first (and unintentional) Enlightened Procedure.&quot; . This was after the character killed a mountain monster in Antarctica. Though maybe the VEs were observing him since some time, due to past activities and interests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 05-19-2021, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}